WEBVTT

00:10.844 --> 00:14.681
If they knew I was coming here,
they could've told me to wear sneakers.

00:15.181 --> 00:18.393
They told me to get all dressed up,
and for what?

00:19.227 --> 00:20.395
My legs are killing me.

00:21.187 --> 00:22.313
Damn it.

00:23.440 --> 00:25.608
Ms. Cha Mu-hee, your mic's going live.

00:25.692 --> 00:26.860
Ah, fuck.

00:27.736 --> 00:29.696
Please hold the action cam upright.

00:35.368 --> 00:36.411
Is this good?

00:38.830 --> 00:40.623
These heels will be ruined.

00:41.458 --> 00:43.668
Hey, is my manager there?

00:44.169 --> 00:45.545
Mu-hee, I'm listening.

00:45.628 --> 00:47.630
Were these shoes a gift or a loan?

00:47.714 --> 00:50.133
Those are on loan.
Please be careful with them.

00:50.216 --> 00:51.468
All right. Okay.

01:47.148 --> 01:49.317
Please track Ms. Cha Mu-hee,
just like that.

02:05.083 --> 02:07.961
Drone one, push in
for a tighter front shot on Ms. Cha.

02:08.628 --> 02:10.380
Park, is in-ear interpretation ready?

02:10.463 --> 02:11.798
Yes, we're good to go.

02:11.881 --> 02:12.715
Mr. Joo.

02:13.383 --> 02:14.384
-Hello.
-Hello.

02:14.467 --> 02:16.469
Add some inserts here and there.

02:17.512 --> 02:19.139
Ms. Cho?

02:22.183 --> 02:24.269
Mr. Joo, are you ready?

02:24.769 --> 02:26.688
Yes, I'm all set too.

02:37.240 --> 02:39.242
Wow, we're so high up.

02:39.826 --> 02:43.913
So, back in the day, all this belonged
to the king who lived in this castle.

02:46.124 --> 02:49.794
Imagine standing here, looking out,
knowing all of this land was yours.

02:51.546 --> 02:53.464
How many acres is all this?

02:55.258 --> 02:56.843
You can't lean on that. Step back.

02:57.760 --> 02:58.595
What's that?

02:59.095 --> 03:01.681
It's not like you
to speak up like this, Mr. Joo.

03:02.265 --> 03:05.059
Are you worried about me?
What, in case I blow away?

03:05.685 --> 03:07.437
It's on the sign in front of you.

03:11.441 --> 03:13.109
"Do not lean or climb on the railing."

03:13.610 --> 03:14.861
I simply translated it.

03:17.113 --> 03:20.325
What about those who don't speak Italian?
It should also be in English.

03:20.950 --> 03:23.620
It is also in English.
You just couldn't read it.

03:24.204 --> 03:25.496
I know English.

03:25.580 --> 03:28.374
I can read my ABCs. Here it is.

03:29.334 --> 03:30.376
That's German.

03:30.460 --> 03:32.003
It's in English below that.

03:34.005 --> 03:36.507
I only mixed them up
because they look so similar.

03:37.008 --> 03:39.469
People who can tell the difference
are the weird ones.

03:42.138 --> 03:43.932
Today's the last day of filming.

03:45.975 --> 03:48.519
I wrote a farewell message
for Hiro in Japanese.

03:48.603 --> 03:50.355
No need to interpret that for me.

03:51.064 --> 03:52.232
All right.

03:54.150 --> 03:55.610
Now, tracking Hiro.

04:12.377 --> 04:13.795
"It's a beautiful day."

04:13.878 --> 04:17.715
"I chose this spot for our final shoot.
I'm glad the weather's cooperating."

04:21.135 --> 04:24.514
"Let's go that way.
The view from over there is even better."

04:25.098 --> 04:26.766
Have you been here before?

04:30.979 --> 04:34.399
"I once filmed a series here,
when I was new to acting."

04:35.108 --> 04:38.569
"I made so many mistakes
that I still remember my lines clearly."

04:39.279 --> 04:41.114
"I was such a terrible actor then."

04:41.197 --> 04:42.198
Really?

04:42.282 --> 04:45.618
How terrible, exactly?
Now I'm curious. Is it on YouTube?

04:45.702 --> 04:48.871
Please don't look it up.
I really don't want to remember.

04:49.539 --> 04:50.581
What was it again?

04:51.416 --> 04:52.542
"Cringewar"?

04:53.584 --> 04:54.669
"Cringeworth"?

04:54.752 --> 04:56.045
"Cringeworth"?

04:56.129 --> 04:57.630
Oh, cringeworthy?

04:57.714 --> 04:58.798
That's it!

04:58.881 --> 05:00.758
-Cringeworthy?
-Cringeworthy!

05:00.842 --> 05:02.135
That's amazing.

05:02.218 --> 05:04.762
They seem closer compared to
when we started shooting.

05:04.846 --> 05:05.680
Don't they?

05:05.763 --> 05:09.726
Now that the trip's almost over,
they're practically besties!

05:29.037 --> 05:29.996
"Beautiful."

05:30.079 --> 05:31.789
"So much that I can't look away."

05:32.749 --> 05:33.583
I agree.

05:36.586 --> 05:39.422
We saw so many beautiful places
while filming.

05:40.089 --> 05:43.551
I'm a little bummed that it's over.

05:45.845 --> 05:47.096
I agree.

05:50.725 --> 05:51.726
I would like…

05:54.979 --> 05:56.647
to keep seeing you.

06:02.070 --> 06:03.905
I think the reason every moment

06:04.655 --> 06:06.657
of our journey has been beautiful…

06:10.244 --> 06:11.829
is that you

06:13.206 --> 06:15.083
were a part of the scenery.

06:29.472 --> 06:30.932
What did he just say?

06:31.516 --> 06:32.392
Can you interpret…

06:33.267 --> 06:34.644
Is he saying goodbye?

06:35.520 --> 06:37.355
Should I give my farewell message now?

06:40.441 --> 06:41.317
Mr. Joo,

06:41.901 --> 06:44.404
if you were too shocked
to interpret what I just said,

06:45.696 --> 06:47.448
can you just pass on

06:48.449 --> 06:49.450
these words to her?

07:16.144 --> 07:17.812
Mr. Joo, what's he saying?

07:19.272 --> 07:21.858
I can't reply
unless you pass on his message.

07:25.278 --> 07:27.572
I guess your farewell message
won't be necessary.

07:28.781 --> 07:30.199
Let me interpret his words.

07:30.908 --> 07:32.326
He asked me to tell you…

07:41.419 --> 07:45.256
"I really like you, Cha Mu-hee."

08:00.313 --> 08:01.397
Did you hear that?

08:02.315 --> 08:04.025
Did the message get through?

08:20.041 --> 08:24.754
CAN THIS LOVE BE TRANSLATED?

08:26.964 --> 08:29.509
JAPAN

08:36.390 --> 08:40.436
Here's the forecast across the country
for Monday, April 8th.

08:40.520 --> 08:42.980
It looks like
more areas will see sunshine today.

08:43.064 --> 08:46.067
Rain is expected
in southern Kanto in the morning,

08:46.150 --> 08:48.152
but skies will gradually clear.

08:48.903 --> 08:51.572
1 YEAR AGO, APRIL

09:09.465 --> 09:13.302
"Let's hear from Mr. Kim Young-hwan,
who is well-loved in Japan too."

09:13.803 --> 09:19.267
I am elated to bring my latest novel
to my Japanese readers.

09:19.767 --> 09:23.938
I hope all of you enjoy it.

09:24.021 --> 09:25.398
Thank you.

09:44.041 --> 09:46.502
They'll now take questions from the press.

09:47.253 --> 09:48.713
You had a big turnout.

09:49.213 --> 09:52.174
See? That's how popular I am.
Only you look down on me.

09:52.258 --> 09:54.302
When have I ever looked down on you?

09:55.511 --> 09:59.140
Anyway, thanks
for putting up with this old man

09:59.223 --> 10:01.267
and interpreting the past few days.

10:02.893 --> 10:03.769
Here.

10:05.062 --> 10:06.522
The publisher gave it to me.

10:07.023 --> 10:09.609
The Japanese are great
at this sort of thing.

10:09.692 --> 10:11.402
Why would you give me your gift?

10:11.485 --> 10:15.656
A Japanese literary magazine is coming
to Seoul next month to interview me.

10:16.157 --> 10:18.117
I'd like you to interpret for me then too.

10:18.951 --> 10:21.954
I'm sorry, but I can't.
I won't be in Seoul then.

10:22.997 --> 10:25.499
Right, you said you're going to Spain,
didn't you?

10:25.583 --> 10:28.711
Yes, I probably won't be back in Korea
for a few months once I leave.

10:29.420 --> 10:30.755
Oh no, that won't do.

10:31.339 --> 10:35.968
You're the only one who can make sense
of my nonsense and interpret it.

10:36.927 --> 10:39.096
Why not delay your Spain trip a little?

10:39.722 --> 10:43.225
So dragging a busy guy to Japan
and making him work wasn't enough?

10:43.309 --> 10:45.186
Aren't you being too shameless?

10:47.271 --> 10:50.650
Then why don't we swing by a sushi bar
before the airport for a drink?

10:50.733 --> 10:53.527
Mr. Kim, please.
Cut down on your drinking.

10:54.028 --> 10:56.322
You kept mixing up
the characters in your novel.

10:56.822 --> 11:00.576
The name of the heroine's first husband
is Nam Hyeon-su, not Park In-cheol.

11:01.160 --> 11:03.245
Yeong-suk's first husband is Nam Hyeon-su?

11:03.329 --> 11:05.247
You're the one who wrote the novel.

11:05.331 --> 11:07.917
I was at a loss
while interpreting there, seriously.

11:08.000 --> 11:12.046
You handled it just fine.
So fine that it's my treat. Let's go.

11:12.129 --> 11:15.466
You can treat me next time.
I have somewhere to visit while I'm here.

11:15.549 --> 11:16.509
Where?

11:17.468 --> 11:20.805
Heading somewhere nice on your own?
Meeting someone?

11:21.764 --> 11:24.517
-Do you have a date?
-Have a safe trip back, Mr. Kim.

11:25.101 --> 11:27.186
Oh, so it is a date, then?

11:27.687 --> 11:30.523
Wow, and here I thought
you had no game whatsoever.

11:31.107 --> 11:33.317
If it's a date,
share those cookies with her.

11:33.401 --> 11:34.652
Nice and sweet!

11:43.911 --> 11:48.082
To transfer to the Enoden Line,
first exit the JR Line using your ticket.

11:48.165 --> 11:51.085
Once you exit, turn right,
and you'll see the central square.

11:51.168 --> 11:52.628
Keep walking past the square,

11:52.712 --> 11:56.006
and when you see this sign,
go through the gates to the left.

12:01.804 --> 12:03.556
-Sorry.
-Sorry.

12:22.658 --> 12:23.743
-Excuse me.
-Yes?

12:23.826 --> 12:25.578
You're out of Korean leaflets.

12:25.661 --> 12:28.205
Oh, sorry. We'll restock them.

12:28.289 --> 12:29.123
Thank you.

14:21.986 --> 14:23.737
Paolo, stop messing around, please.

14:24.822 --> 14:27.032
It's all right.
He didn't do it on purpose.

14:27.116 --> 14:29.201
Wow! You speak Italian.

14:29.285 --> 14:31.996
We've never met a Japanese person
who speaks Italian.

14:32.079 --> 14:35.124
I'm not Japanese. I'm Korean.

14:35.207 --> 14:37.585
-Really?
-Oh, Korean?

14:37.668 --> 14:40.421
-Have you ever been to Italy?
-Yes, I have.

14:41.881 --> 14:43.591
"Hashtag, Momo-chan Ramen."

14:44.091 --> 14:45.342
"Hashtag, a fresh start."

14:45.426 --> 14:47.136
"Hashtag, grateful for you."

14:47.219 --> 14:49.430
I must say, your Italian is very good.

14:49.513 --> 14:53.183
"Hashtag, will make you happy."

15:12.620 --> 15:14.038
Excuse me.

15:14.955 --> 15:16.749
The food is hot. Here you go.

15:16.832 --> 15:17.917
Thank you.

15:18.000 --> 15:19.668
Let me know if you need anything.

15:19.752 --> 15:21.337
Can kids eat this?

15:21.420 --> 15:24.214
Yes, but kids might find it a bit spicy.

15:24.298 --> 15:25.257
Welcome.

15:25.758 --> 15:27.343
Please sit anywhere you'd like.

15:33.390 --> 15:34.600
Ma'am?

15:36.602 --> 15:37.561
Please.

15:44.818 --> 15:46.028
Excuse me.

15:46.695 --> 15:48.072
Here's our menu.

15:54.995 --> 15:58.457
Are you Momo-chan,
the owner of Momo-chan Ramen?

16:05.714 --> 16:06.674
Yes.

16:14.598 --> 16:17.434
Okay, one Momo-chan Ramen coming right up.

16:17.935 --> 16:19.103
Excuse me.

16:19.186 --> 16:22.856
I would recommend that you order… this.

16:22.940 --> 16:24.942
Okay, thank you.

16:27.903 --> 16:29.947
She looked older in the photos.

16:45.087 --> 16:49.633
I am here in search of a Korean man
who wishes to have

16:50.134 --> 16:52.261
a fresh start with you, Momo-chan.

17:07.901 --> 17:10.654
It sounds too much like a news anchor.

17:12.114 --> 17:14.491
Isn't there an option
to change the tone of voice?

17:14.575 --> 17:15.909
Make it a little tougher?

17:23.834 --> 17:26.420
Oh, he's Chinese?

17:27.171 --> 17:28.672
I thought he was Korean.

17:31.216 --> 17:33.594
First, let's give you a female voice.

17:34.845 --> 17:36.680
I need you to interpret well.

17:39.058 --> 17:40.559
Can this app swear too?

17:44.897 --> 17:45.898
Fuck.

17:49.818 --> 17:51.028
Fuck.

17:59.161 --> 18:00.162
KakaoTalk?

18:01.038 --> 18:02.372
You're Korean?

18:09.755 --> 18:11.090
You understood everything?

18:12.758 --> 18:14.510
You did, didn't you?

18:16.428 --> 18:17.429
I happened to hear.

18:17.513 --> 18:20.516
You were eavesdropping
while pretending to be Chinese.

18:20.599 --> 18:22.559
When did I ever pretend to be Chinese?

18:23.352 --> 18:26.146
You were pretending
to read that Chinese pamphlet.

18:26.230 --> 18:29.525
I wasn't pretending. I was reading it.
I don't just read the Chinese one.

18:30.818 --> 18:33.195
I always read the English,
French, and Italian ones.

18:33.278 --> 18:35.405
Come on, don't be ridiculous.

18:35.489 --> 18:36.949
What are you, Papago?

18:37.032 --> 18:37.866
Look here, I--

18:37.950 --> 18:38.992
Paolo!

18:40.077 --> 18:40.911
Paolo!

18:41.578 --> 18:43.497
Our son is sick. Please call an ambulance.

18:43.580 --> 18:44.790
We don't speak Japanese.

18:44.873 --> 18:46.125
What happened to him?

18:46.208 --> 18:47.251
He has an allergy.

18:47.334 --> 18:50.462
Something in his snack earlier
must have triggered a reaction.

18:50.546 --> 18:51.630
An ambulance, please.

18:51.713 --> 18:54.383
Please tell them
a boy is having an allergic reaction.

18:54.466 --> 18:55.300
Okay.

18:55.384 --> 18:57.010
What snack did he eat?

18:57.761 --> 18:58.720
Here.

19:00.139 --> 19:01.181
This one.

19:01.265 --> 19:03.433
You'd better take this with you
to the hospital.

19:03.517 --> 19:04.434
Okay.

19:04.518 --> 19:05.853
I called an ambulance.

19:05.936 --> 19:08.230
But the alleyway here is narrow.

19:08.313 --> 19:10.023
It may be a while before they arrive.

19:10.107 --> 19:14.611
She says the alley's too narrow,
so the ambulance might take a while.

19:14.695 --> 19:17.489
-I'll carry him to the main street.
-Okay, honey.

19:18.073 --> 19:19.116
I'll carry him.

19:19.700 --> 19:21.118
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

19:23.162 --> 19:25.789
Tell the ambulance to meet us
at the main street entrance.

19:25.873 --> 19:26.707
Okay.

19:29.209 --> 19:30.711
I'll watch your things.

19:30.794 --> 19:32.171
Okay, thank you.

19:39.469 --> 19:41.346
So he really is Papago.

19:46.852 --> 19:47.936
Excuse me.

19:48.645 --> 19:49.479
Excuse me.

19:55.319 --> 19:58.030
I let the paramedics know
what's going on with Paolo.

19:58.655 --> 20:02.618
Give me a call if you need
additional interpretation at the hospital.

20:02.701 --> 20:03.660
Thank you so much.

20:04.453 --> 20:06.121
-Please take care of him.
-Got it.

20:08.749 --> 20:11.585
Turning left soon. Please be careful.

20:23.889 --> 20:24.806
Thank you.

20:30.354 --> 20:31.688
Can you help me too?

20:33.190 --> 20:35.025
I have an emergency too.

20:35.525 --> 20:37.653
I was going to use Papago,

20:37.736 --> 20:40.322
but I think a human voice
will be better than AI

20:40.405 --> 20:42.908
at conveying my feelings
in a more authentic way.

20:42.991 --> 20:45.494
I don't want to interpret
a sordid lovers' quarrel.

20:47.162 --> 20:49.331
I knew it. You heard everything.

20:49.915 --> 20:51.166
-Fuck.
-F…

20:51.250 --> 20:52.584
You heard that too, right?

20:53.210 --> 20:54.211
I happened to hear.

20:57.756 --> 21:01.260
Then you'll know I'm here to beg
a man who's starting over to take me back.

21:02.135 --> 21:03.387
Please help me.

21:04.054 --> 21:05.472
If he rejects me via Papago,

21:06.890 --> 21:09.017
I'll feel unbearably pathetic.

21:14.606 --> 21:15.983
Fine. I'll help you.

21:16.566 --> 21:18.735
But I'm not interpreting any profanity.

21:25.909 --> 21:28.412
She says Mr. Kim Yu-jin isn't here
but in Tokyo.

21:29.204 --> 21:30.205
He's not here?

21:31.123 --> 21:33.375
Or maybe he saw me and hid.

21:34.751 --> 21:36.795
I feel like
the two of them are lying to me.

21:37.921 --> 21:40.215
So what? You want me to tell her that?

21:41.591 --> 21:42.426
Forget it.

21:44.011 --> 21:45.929
Just ask her when he'll be back.

21:55.188 --> 21:57.691
She says she'll call over his girlfriend.

21:59.026 --> 21:59.860
Excuse me?

21:59.943 --> 22:02.321
Eiko, can you come out here for a moment?

22:04.781 --> 22:06.950
Is she really the one
he's starting over with?

22:08.243 --> 22:09.286
It is!

22:11.705 --> 22:15.208
He even posted her photo on Instagram,
calling it "a fresh start." Look.

22:15.292 --> 22:16.668
It's her, isn't it?

22:26.845 --> 22:28.472
You guessed wrong.

22:29.139 --> 22:30.098
No way…

22:31.683 --> 22:34.561
I naturally thought
it was the younger woman in the photo.

22:49.034 --> 22:50.786
Could you just ask her

22:51.661 --> 22:52.913
how far along she is?

22:58.627 --> 23:00.087
Seven months, she says.

23:02.005 --> 23:04.257
He broke up with me three months ago.

23:04.341 --> 23:05.300
Seven months…

23:07.844 --> 23:09.262
I must have been crazy.

23:09.846 --> 23:11.640
That absolute douchebag!

23:14.893 --> 23:15.977
Excuse me.

23:18.230 --> 23:20.816
Is she Ms. Cha Mu-hee?

23:21.900 --> 23:23.026
Probably.

23:23.110 --> 23:26.947
I have something I'd like to say to her.
Could you pass it on for me?

23:31.952 --> 23:32.911
Excuse me!

23:33.787 --> 23:34.746
Excuse me!

23:38.375 --> 23:41.962
Can you type this in Japanese for me?
"The Korean chef here is a dirtbag."

23:42.045 --> 23:45.090
Hashtag two-timer,
hashtag cheater, hashtag manwh…

23:45.924 --> 23:49.386
Die. I'm going to curse you!
I hope you go out of business!

23:49.886 --> 23:53.098
As with profanity, I don't translate
curses wishing ill on others.

23:53.932 --> 23:55.642
I'd rather not get involved,

23:55.725 --> 23:58.770
but the woman asked me to pass on
a message, so I'll do that much.

24:03.525 --> 24:05.652
The father of my child

24:06.153 --> 24:08.029
is my ex-husband, not Yu-jin.

24:10.365 --> 24:12.451
Even though I knew it was selfish,

24:13.243 --> 24:15.537
I wanted to rely on his kindness.

24:17.622 --> 24:22.085
But if Ms. Cha Mu-hee
is able to change his mind,

24:23.420 --> 24:25.338
I'd happily let him go.

24:27.924 --> 24:30.719
She told me to take him?
Could you have misheard?

24:31.303 --> 24:32.554
I passed on what I heard.

24:33.889 --> 24:34.848
What's her deal?

24:35.348 --> 24:37.809
Is she mocking me?
Like "Take him if you can"?

24:37.893 --> 24:38.977
How did it seem to you?

24:39.060 --> 24:40.645
I just relayed the message.

24:40.729 --> 24:43.064
No, I mean,
do you really think she meant it?

24:43.148 --> 24:44.441
It's too suspicious!

24:44.524 --> 24:46.693
She's in a rough spot,
but she's being nice!

24:46.776 --> 24:50.822
I only pass along the words people say,
not judge what kind of person they are.

24:50.906 --> 24:54.159
Fine. We'll go back together and see.
Let's go, Mr. Papago.

24:54.242 --> 24:55.410
That's enough!

24:55.911 --> 24:57.537
Ms. Cha… Mu-hee?

24:59.956 --> 25:04.044
If you'd broken up, it's not betrayal.
And it's not his baby, so he didn't cheat.

25:05.045 --> 25:06.213
They're just two people--

25:06.296 --> 25:09.090
In love… is what you're saying.

25:10.800 --> 25:12.552
-That pisses me off.
-Exactly.

25:13.887 --> 25:16.348
Go any further,
and you become the bad guy.

25:16.431 --> 25:19.351
Whether I end up the bad guy
or a crazy bitch, I'll deal with it.

25:19.434 --> 25:21.520
-I just need you to interpret.
-I refuse.

25:22.437 --> 25:26.441
Usually, if you want to act bad or crazy,
the act of destruction itself

25:26.525 --> 25:29.528
is enough to convey
just how pissed off you really are.

25:29.611 --> 25:32.989
No interpretation needed.
Or use a language that's universal.

25:36.368 --> 25:37.494
Best of luck.

25:39.120 --> 25:41.581
You said you don't judge,
so why am I the bad guy?

25:45.961 --> 25:47.754
So their love is pure and sweet,

25:48.338 --> 25:50.257
but mine has to end a mess, with this?

25:56.096 --> 25:58.765
He told me he was breaking up with me
and vanished.

25:59.307 --> 26:02.143
He's done it before, so I just waited.

26:02.644 --> 26:05.814
But three months later,
he posted a photo saying "a fresh start."

26:05.897 --> 26:07.482
That's why I came here to find him.

26:09.568 --> 26:12.779
It may seem desperate and pathetic,
but this is love too.

26:13.989 --> 26:15.574
I don't want to end it with this.

26:21.329 --> 26:23.832
Help me end things
with a shred of dignity.

26:27.294 --> 26:29.004
Please translate my love too.

26:31.673 --> 26:32.924
I beg you.

26:37.846 --> 26:39.556
Hey, Yu-jin.

26:40.640 --> 26:42.726
Yes, everything is fine here.

26:43.977 --> 26:45.395
You'll be back tonight?

26:47.230 --> 26:49.608
No, I wouldn't want you to hurry.

26:49.691 --> 26:52.068
Come back tomorrow as scheduled.

26:52.694 --> 26:53.653
Yes.

26:54.154 --> 26:56.781
Okay, see you tomorrow.

27:03.997 --> 27:06.833
Sorry, but we're closed…

27:14.299 --> 27:17.427
I appreciate your kind heart.

27:18.053 --> 27:19.304
But I came back

27:19.387 --> 27:21.598
because there's something
I want to ask you.

27:30.106 --> 27:32.150
While I was dating him,

27:32.651 --> 27:35.236
he'd go off the grid from time to time,

27:35.737 --> 27:37.822
for anything from a week
to over two months.

27:39.282 --> 27:40.950
Was he with you during those times?

27:48.750 --> 27:49.668
So he was.

27:51.336 --> 27:54.506
So he really did cheat.
He really did betray me.

28:03.723 --> 28:06.643
She said he comforted and helped her
in her time of need.

28:08.812 --> 28:10.897
You shouldn't sugarcoat what he did.

28:10.980 --> 28:13.191
What, was he helping the needy?
Is she a beggar?

28:13.274 --> 28:16.111
If pity is what made him stay,
that's like begging to be loved.

28:17.862 --> 28:21.199
I'll take that as angry self-talk
and leave those words untranslated.

28:21.825 --> 28:24.285
You said you wanted
to keep your dignity intact.

28:32.752 --> 28:35.797
Still, he always found his way back to me.

28:37.257 --> 28:40.802
I guess he won't be able to
now that you're a soon-to-be single mom.

28:40.885 --> 28:44.264
Not that I'd take him back if he did.

28:47.183 --> 28:50.854
Since you won't translate profanity,
let's go with some words of encouragement.

28:54.607 --> 28:56.776
It may be love gained from misfortune,

28:58.445 --> 28:59.904
but I hope you're happy.

29:11.416 --> 29:13.084
She wants you to hear her out.

29:15.754 --> 29:20.759
Actually, Yu-jin and I were dating
when he was studying in Japan.

29:21.801 --> 29:25.430
But his heart was stolen by another woman.

29:29.601 --> 29:33.188
She was abandoned by her family

29:33.271 --> 29:36.858
and had no one to turn to,
helpless in a miserable situation.

29:38.276 --> 29:39.360
It was as if

29:40.612 --> 29:45.366
she were the tragic heroine of a movie,
weighed down by a burden of misery.

29:45.992 --> 29:48.620
Every time, I would try to make him stay,

29:49.954 --> 29:52.665
but he still left,
saying he couldn't leave her alone.

29:56.044 --> 29:59.214
Who is she talking about?

30:03.593 --> 30:05.220
That woman is you.

30:07.931 --> 30:09.390
What did she just say?

30:11.309 --> 30:12.185
What did she say?

30:14.103 --> 30:16.147
The one who used their misery to be loved

30:17.357 --> 30:18.608
is you.

30:23.321 --> 30:26.825
Even after realizing her man betrayed her,
she still came all this way.

30:27.492 --> 30:32.080
She must have been really lonely
to throw away her pride like this.

30:34.457 --> 30:36.751
-Hey.
-Don't say a word. I got the gist.

30:39.921 --> 30:43.258
I have no intention
of understanding this woman's words

30:43.842 --> 30:45.718
and making the face she wants to see.

30:45.802 --> 30:47.220
Then what do you want to do?

30:48.763 --> 30:49.764
I don't know.

30:51.349 --> 30:53.184
But I think I'm about to cry.

30:55.937 --> 30:59.190
If I end up crying in front of that woman,
I'll die of humiliation.

31:16.207 --> 31:18.710
Then stay like this,
and I'll sort things out.

31:18.793 --> 31:20.753
With as much dignity as possible.

31:23.214 --> 31:25.216
There seems to have been
a misunderstanding.

31:25.300 --> 31:27.176
She and I are traveling together.

31:27.260 --> 31:29.429
We just dropped by to say hello.

31:30.179 --> 31:32.765
Sorry? The two of you
are traveling together?

31:36.436 --> 31:37.896
We brought a gift from Tokyo.

31:39.814 --> 31:43.484
She was just trying to be polite,
yet you have been incredibly rude.

31:44.485 --> 31:48.031
What you just said will stay with me.

31:49.073 --> 31:51.826
I won't pass along any words
that may hurt her.

31:57.123 --> 31:59.375
If you're better now, let's go.

32:46.130 --> 32:48.883
Thank you so much for your help today.

32:51.970 --> 32:54.764
-In case I got anything on you earlier.
-I'm fine.

32:56.808 --> 32:59.185
That gift looked pricey.
How much was it? I'll pay.

32:59.268 --> 33:00.395
It was gifted to me too.

33:01.521 --> 33:02.480
Really?

33:03.731 --> 33:05.316
Still, I feel really bad.

33:07.360 --> 33:09.946
Should I treat you to a meal?
We both skipped lunch.

33:11.072 --> 33:12.907
I'm really okay.

33:16.035 --> 33:17.704
-Don't worry about it.
-Okay.

33:20.623 --> 33:21.624
Take care.

33:26.879 --> 33:28.423
About today.

33:29.007 --> 33:32.468
Thank you, and I'm sorry.

33:34.804 --> 33:35.972
Enjoy your trip.

33:39.976 --> 33:41.519
Thank you.

33:51.654 --> 33:53.656
She still came all this way.

33:54.490 --> 33:58.786
She must have been really lonely
to throw away her pride like this.

34:03.291 --> 34:04.709
-Yes, thanks.
-Thank you.

34:17.430 --> 34:19.932
A woman weighed down
by a burden of misery?

34:22.226 --> 34:23.644
Doesn't seem that way to me.

34:27.398 --> 34:28.566
Here you go.

34:30.151 --> 34:31.319
Thanks.

35:01.349 --> 35:04.143
Excuse me?

35:05.394 --> 35:07.897
-I forgot to give you your phone back.
-What is it now?

35:07.980 --> 35:11.067
-You just got a call from a foreigner.
-Right.

35:13.319 --> 35:14.487
Yes, hello.

35:14.570 --> 35:19.158
My son is fine, thanks to your help.
Thank you so much.

35:19.659 --> 35:20.868
I'm glad to hear that.

35:20.952 --> 35:23.704
We'd like to give you a gift as thanks.

35:24.372 --> 35:26.124
There's no need.

35:26.207 --> 35:27.875
We had a dinner reservation,

35:27.959 --> 35:31.671
but we won't be able to go
as we need to stay at the hospital.

35:31.754 --> 35:33.756
The reservation is for two people.

35:33.840 --> 35:38.302
If the person who answered is a friend
of yours, you could go with her.

35:42.890 --> 35:44.392
Right, friend…

35:44.475 --> 35:48.187
The reservation was hard to get,
and it's already paid for.

35:48.271 --> 35:50.398
We'd love for you to go.

35:52.275 --> 35:54.944
Okay, then. I will.

35:55.444 --> 35:56.445
Thank you very much.

35:57.280 --> 35:59.574
Yes. Okay, thank you.

36:00.074 --> 36:01.159
Goodbye.

36:08.624 --> 36:10.126
That was Italian, wasn't it?

36:10.918 --> 36:11.752
Yes.

36:11.836 --> 36:14.505
It must be that kid from earlier.
Is he okay?

36:15.298 --> 36:18.009
Thankfully, he's recovering.

36:18.092 --> 36:19.844
Thank goodness.

36:20.803 --> 36:24.140
And thank goodness
I didn't take off with your phone.

36:24.640 --> 36:25.975
Today's a lucky day.

36:34.859 --> 36:35.860
Ms. Cha Mu-hee.

36:36.861 --> 36:38.988
What are you going to do now? Any plans?

36:39.572 --> 36:42.825
I've already done what I came here to do.
As you saw.

36:42.909 --> 36:43.784
Why?

36:44.285 --> 36:46.370
Then would you like to join me for dinner?

36:52.293 --> 36:55.171
-Earlier, you said you didn't want to.
-I never said that.

36:55.254 --> 36:56.714
I simply didn't see a need to.

36:58.007 --> 36:59.091
So what's changed?

37:00.885 --> 37:03.471
That Italian family treated me to dinner.

37:03.554 --> 37:06.432
It's for two people,
and it'd be a waste to go by myself.

37:06.515 --> 37:08.935
That would be a waste.
Is it at an expensive place?

37:09.018 --> 37:10.394
Probably.

37:14.065 --> 37:16.651
Then I'll come and do you a favor
as my thanks.

37:20.154 --> 37:24.158
I'm the one doing you a favor,
so why act like it's the other way around?

37:24.242 --> 37:25.368
Oh please.

37:25.451 --> 37:28.955
Good food is never as good or as filling
when eaten alone.

37:29.038 --> 37:31.958
-Let's go. Should we take a cab?
-The reservation is at 7:00.

37:37.713 --> 37:40.883
Then should we meet
outside the restaurant at 7:00?

37:45.388 --> 37:46.722
Let's hang out until then.

37:47.515 --> 37:48.849
If you're okay with that.

37:50.893 --> 37:52.228
What should we do until then?

37:55.064 --> 37:57.608
Well, this is a tourist spot,

37:58.192 --> 37:59.402
so let's go sightseeing.

38:02.613 --> 38:04.240
I know it's a bit late,

38:05.157 --> 38:06.450
but what's your name?

38:06.534 --> 38:07.576
Joo Ho-jin.

38:07.660 --> 38:09.328
Nice to meet you, Mr. Joo Ho-jin.

38:10.454 --> 38:12.331
I'm Cha Mu-hee.

38:12.415 --> 38:14.875
Yes, I know.
Nice to meet you, Ms. Cha Mu-hee.

38:25.177 --> 38:28.931
We're heading to Enoshima next. Off we go!

38:39.317 --> 38:40.401
NA JIN-SUK

38:47.658 --> 38:49.410
You're an actor?

38:49.493 --> 38:51.120
So you're a celebrity?

38:52.413 --> 38:55.207
Not every celebrity is famous.

38:55.708 --> 38:57.001
That only applies

38:57.752 --> 38:59.712
to the top 5%, I suppose.

39:02.131 --> 39:05.259
But you can totally look me up online.

39:08.179 --> 39:09.805
What? Right.

39:13.225 --> 39:15.853
Wow, you've been in a lot of stuff.

39:17.688 --> 39:20.149
You were in the movie The Crooks?
I've seen that.

39:21.901 --> 39:24.070
I bet you're wondering
which scenes I was in.

39:24.862 --> 39:27.114
I get it. I only appeared
for a split second.

39:28.032 --> 39:30.618
I felt embarrassed
to include it in my filmography,

39:31.118 --> 39:34.372
but my agent called the search engine
and urged them to add it.

39:34.455 --> 39:37.958
Either way, over ten million people
saw a movie you were in.

39:38.834 --> 39:40.711
So what? Nobody knows I was in it.

39:43.422 --> 39:47.718
There might be fireworks and celebrations,
but the festival isn't for me.

39:48.344 --> 39:51.180
It's only for the people in the limelight.

39:53.849 --> 39:55.393
Like that woman said,

39:55.476 --> 39:58.270
I'm an unlucky actress
who's never seen success.

39:59.438 --> 40:01.774
If she's right,
you'll be successful from now on.

40:04.985 --> 40:09.990
If a man who's drawn to misfortune
has left you,

40:10.825 --> 40:13.494
that must mean
happiness is all that awaits you.

40:19.750 --> 40:23.546
You're good at interpreting,
but even better at reframing things.

40:45.276 --> 40:47.653
It said "top-ranked."
A little further this way.

40:51.615 --> 40:55.786
A NEW START. A FESTIVAL WITH FIREWORKS!
WITH #PAPAGO #GRATEFUL_FOR_YOU

41:00.583 --> 41:02.334
Aren't you gonna take any photos?

41:03.210 --> 41:04.462
Don't you have Instagram?

41:04.962 --> 41:07.506
I do, but I rarely post.

41:08.007 --> 41:12.136
I have 9,989 followers.

41:13.471 --> 41:14.388
A shame, isn't it?

41:15.764 --> 41:16.640
What is?

41:17.141 --> 41:19.143
Just a few more, and I'd be at 10,000.

41:20.144 --> 41:21.770
I just can't seem to hit it.

41:23.189 --> 41:24.523
You want me to follow you?

41:25.900 --> 41:28.360
Come on, it's not much to ask.
Let's be mutuals.

41:28.444 --> 41:30.779
-I don't follow many people.
-I'll consider it.

41:30.863 --> 41:33.324
I'd be nervous being mutuals
with a celebrity.

41:33.908 --> 41:36.452
I'm not famous enough
for you to feel nervous.

41:36.952 --> 41:37.953
Well, who knows?

41:38.037 --> 41:41.790
You could blow up, just like you said,
and hit ten million followers.

41:42.291 --> 41:44.335
Then they'd come
snooping around my account.

41:47.046 --> 41:50.716
You have a knack for saying no
in the most flattering way possible.

41:53.469 --> 41:54.887
We should head back down.

41:56.388 --> 42:00.476
The view from that observatory is great,
but we'd be late for dinner.

42:01.810 --> 42:03.395
Have you been here before?

42:03.979 --> 42:04.939
Yes.

42:05.481 --> 42:06.815
And you're here again?

42:07.441 --> 42:08.275
By yourself?

42:09.735 --> 42:11.487
There's a legend on this island.

42:11.570 --> 42:15.574
The legend says the dragon god of the sea
fell for a maiden from the heavens

42:15.658 --> 42:17.952
and made this island as a gift for her.

42:19.828 --> 42:21.455
I guess he really went all out.

42:22.206 --> 42:23.707
The person I came here with

42:23.791 --> 42:26.126
said they wanted this island
for their birthday too.

42:26.627 --> 42:29.838
Today happens to be their birthday,
so I thought I'd stop by.

42:32.675 --> 42:34.927
An island as a birthday gift?

42:36.011 --> 42:38.305
They wanted you here on their birthday?

42:38.389 --> 42:40.224
That's a confession. Was it a woman?

42:44.353 --> 42:47.523
Come on. You witnessed
every detail of my pathetic love life.

42:48.023 --> 42:49.191
It's only fair you spill.

42:49.275 --> 42:51.610
Why would I share any of that
with a stranger?

42:51.694 --> 42:53.487
That's exactly why you would!

42:53.571 --> 42:55.906
You can speak freely,
since we'll never see each other again.

42:56.407 --> 42:58.742
That's why I'm not embarrassed at all.

43:04.123 --> 43:05.583
It was a very long time ago.

43:06.500 --> 43:07.793
And back then,

43:08.294 --> 43:11.797
I pretended not to understand her,
the same way you did earlier.

43:15.050 --> 43:19.305
She confessed in a roundabout way
and probably thought you rejected her.

43:22.308 --> 43:25.436
Why not ask her to join you here now?
You said today is her birthday.

43:26.645 --> 43:29.106
She has someone else
to spend birthdays with now.

43:36.864 --> 43:37.990
Come on. We'll be late.

43:43.787 --> 43:45.039
Wait for me.

44:04.975 --> 44:06.810
I think we're almost there.

44:06.894 --> 44:08.896
Can't we just ask a passerby
for directions?

44:08.979 --> 44:10.606
You even speak Japanese.

44:10.689 --> 44:12.566
No.

44:14.902 --> 44:16.570
I think I know where it is now.

44:18.238 --> 44:20.157
It's just two more blocks this way.

44:20.240 --> 44:21.241
But

44:21.909 --> 44:23.410
we keep going in circles.

44:25.162 --> 44:27.289
-I think it's this way.
-Hey, stop. Wait there.

44:32.920 --> 44:36.382
I think the restaurant's this way,
not that way.

44:37.424 --> 44:39.426
-It's this way.
-Wanna bet?

44:40.344 --> 44:41.970
If I win, you have to follow me.

44:42.054 --> 44:44.139
Is getting 10,000 followers
that important?

44:44.223 --> 44:46.767
It is to me. So you agree to the bet?

44:55.109 --> 44:56.443
Excuse me.

44:57.611 --> 44:58.862
Restaurant.

44:58.946 --> 45:00.447
-Hey, Jin-suk.
-That way?

45:00.531 --> 45:01.782
-I'm in Japan.
-This way?

45:01.865 --> 45:04.451
Hey. It's Ji-sun's birthday today,

45:04.952 --> 45:06.995
but we had a fight,
and now I can't reach her.

45:07.496 --> 45:10.290
I just saw her post on Instagram.
Looks like she's in Japan.

45:10.374 --> 45:13.293
Can you check
and see if you can tell where exactly?

45:18.716 --> 45:19.967
-It's that way.
-This way?

45:20.467 --> 45:22.386
Thank… Thank you.

45:24.388 --> 45:27.266
Hey! The restaurant is this way.

45:27.349 --> 45:28.559
Yes! I win.

45:35.149 --> 45:36.150
What's the matter?

45:37.151 --> 45:38.861
The person whose birthday is today

45:39.611 --> 45:40.821
is there on that island.

45:42.573 --> 45:43.699
That's great!

45:43.782 --> 45:46.869
Go! Hurry up and go to her! I'll be fine.

45:49.163 --> 45:51.415
This is an opportunity.

45:51.915 --> 45:54.877
If you waste it,
you'll end up here again, all alone.

45:57.921 --> 45:59.339
No playing dumb this time.

46:00.632 --> 46:01.842
Then things will change.

46:36.710 --> 46:37.711
He went.

46:42.716 --> 46:44.802
It's a shame I don't even have his number.

46:54.645 --> 46:56.271
I wonder if he'll follow me.

47:14.790 --> 47:19.962
This is an announcement
for visitors to Enoshima Observatory.

47:44.820 --> 47:47.406
NA JIN-SUK

48:37.748 --> 48:38.749
Who is it?

48:42.920 --> 48:44.254
Room service.

48:57.225 --> 48:58.810
Have a pleasant evening.

49:21.416 --> 49:22.626
Cut, okay!

49:22.709 --> 49:24.086
We're good!

49:29.841 --> 49:31.176
Pretty good, right?

49:31.259 --> 49:32.928
The scenes are much gorier

49:33.720 --> 49:36.223
than how they were written in the script.

49:37.641 --> 49:41.812
But the background music will be very…
How should I describe it?

49:41.895 --> 49:44.731
Really bright and upbeat.
Sounds fun, doesn't it?

49:45.232 --> 49:46.566
Right, sure!

49:49.945 --> 49:51.863
Today's the last day of filming,

49:53.198 --> 49:54.574
and our film will be a hit.

49:55.492 --> 49:57.202
Our lead character, Do Ra-mi!

49:57.703 --> 49:59.454
-You got this!
-I got this!

50:00.539 --> 50:02.874
I should get back.
That rib cage is so cute.

50:06.837 --> 50:07.754
Mu-hee.

50:08.255 --> 50:09.506
Today's our last day,

50:09.589 --> 50:11.758
but I still don't get
what this movie is about.

50:12.259 --> 50:14.344
Is this a horror movie or a comedy?

50:16.513 --> 50:20.726
Our director is a genius.
Don't you dare try to judge his art.

50:21.226 --> 50:24.021
I'm just worried
since it's your first lead role.

50:24.521 --> 50:25.772
Even your name's weird.

50:25.856 --> 50:27.983
"Do Ra-mi"?
"Do Re-mi" would make more sense.

50:30.861 --> 50:32.154
If this were an obvious hit,

50:32.237 --> 50:34.573
the role of Do Ra-mi
wouldn't have come to me.

50:35.866 --> 50:38.201
I'll just give it my all
until the very end.

50:39.161 --> 50:42.080
-Today might not be our last day.
-We ask for your understanding.

50:42.164 --> 50:45.625
The director argued with the stunt team,
so it might be called off.

50:45.709 --> 50:48.086
We'll move quickly
so we can shoot everything, okay?

50:48.170 --> 50:50.380
That makes no sense!
We're the ones setting up.

50:50.464 --> 50:51.715
They're at it again.

50:51.798 --> 50:54.593
-Please calm down a bit and--
-You're telling me to calm down?

50:54.676 --> 50:58.055
Faster isn't necessarily better.
I'm just asking for more time to prepare.

50:58.138 --> 51:00.265
I told you before.
We can't do all this today!

51:15.447 --> 51:17.157
I, well…

51:18.241 --> 51:21.703
Thanks for doing the stunt yourself.
It's a tough scene.

51:21.787 --> 51:24.790
Of course I should do it.
This is the most important scene.

51:26.249 --> 51:27.918
And it's the last day of filming.

51:28.001 --> 51:30.837
I swear we'll do this in one take,
just like we promised.

51:31.338 --> 51:32.172
Good.

51:33.590 --> 51:34.424
Be careful.

51:36.259 --> 51:37.260
Just relax.

51:41.181 --> 51:42.933
The fireworks festival starts at 9:00.

51:43.016 --> 51:46.645
Let's all pick up the pace
so we can wrap this up before then.

51:51.358 --> 51:52.275
Yes.

51:53.110 --> 51:54.069
Okay, ready?

51:54.152 --> 51:55.612
Here we go.

52:02.410 --> 52:04.496
HOTEL DIAMORTE

52:15.173 --> 52:17.008
HOTEL DI E

52:20.679 --> 52:21.805
Cut, okay!

52:21.888 --> 52:22.931
We're good!

52:23.431 --> 52:24.766
That's a wrap!

52:25.559 --> 52:26.643
Great work, everyone!

52:26.726 --> 52:28.645
Hey, reel in the stunt wire!

52:28.728 --> 52:31.231
-Great job. Thank you.
-Thanks for all your work.

52:39.865 --> 52:41.116
Mu-hee!

53:18.069 --> 53:21.364
As I shut my eyes for what I thought
would be my last moments,

53:21.990 --> 53:23.158
elsewhere,

53:23.825 --> 53:26.328
they were busy
enjoying a festival of their own.

53:27.412 --> 53:30.207
My life had been
entirely devoid of fireworks,

53:31.458 --> 53:35.045
and here they were,
exploding in the distant sky.

53:36.463 --> 53:37.672
How beautiful.

53:44.763 --> 53:45.847
It pisses me off.

54:11.915 --> 54:12.958
Ms. Cha Mu-hee?

54:15.210 --> 54:16.253
Ms. Cha Mu-hee?

54:38.483 --> 54:40.610
You're finally awake, Ms. Cha Mu-hee.

54:41.111 --> 54:42.028
Congratulations.

54:57.335 --> 54:59.713
Ms. Cha Mu-hee has regained consciousness.

54:59.796 --> 55:03.717
The whole world rooted for Do Ra-mi,
and now she's back with us.

55:05.176 --> 55:09.139
To our relief, she immediately recognized
everyone around her

55:09.222 --> 55:11.099
and has no problems communicating.

55:11.182 --> 55:15.145
The Korean actress Cha Mu-hee,
who sparked the Do Ra-mi craze worldwide,

55:15.228 --> 55:17.647
has finally regained consciousness.

55:17.731 --> 55:21.860
Last July, Ms. Cha fell from a rooftop
while filming The Quiet Woman.

55:25.363 --> 55:27.824
…came out of a coma after six months.

55:27.907 --> 55:29.909
The actress suffered a serious accident

55:29.993 --> 55:33.288
when she fell from a roof
while filming the movie The Quiet Woman.

55:56.853 --> 56:00.857
The Korean actress Cha Mu-hee,
who sparked the Do Ra-mi craze worldwide,

56:00.940 --> 56:03.276
has finally regained consciousness.

56:08.782 --> 56:11.409
I had simply closed my eyes
for a brief moment,

56:12.911 --> 56:15.413
but in the world laid before me
when I reopened them,

56:16.581 --> 56:18.249
for the first time in my life,

56:19.084 --> 56:22.087
a lavish festival
was being held just for me.

56:22.837 --> 56:25.006
Ms. Cha, who's made a miraculous recovery,

56:25.090 --> 56:28.093
is said to be experiencing
no cognitive issues

56:28.176 --> 56:31.137
and, barring any lingering aftereffects,
should be able to resume…

56:31.221 --> 56:33.431
You're finally awake, Ms. Cha Mu-hee.

56:34.516 --> 56:37.519
Fans around the world are hoping
Ms. Cha's condition improves

56:37.602 --> 56:40.605
and that she makes a return
to the big screen soon…

57:00.500 --> 57:02.001
And my festival

57:02.502 --> 57:05.588
ended up shaking his life to the core.

57:13.930 --> 57:16.891
CAN THIS LOVE BE TRANSLATED?

59:37.156 --> 59:42.161
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi
